","desc":"The minimum university requirement for a PhD minor is 20 units of History coursework at Stanford’s graduate level (courses numbered 300 and above). All units should be in a single field. Units taken for the minor can be counted as part of the overall requirement for the PhD of 135 units taken at Stanford. Courses used for a minor may not be used to meet the requirements for a master’s degree.\nDegree Requirements\nTwenty units of history coursework at the graduate level (HISTORY 300-399W and 400-499X) at Stanford. All units should be in a single field.\nOptional Courses for the Minor\nThe major and minor departments must approve a PhD minor form outlining the program of study.","t":"text","info":true}],"kind":"info"}]}